menu "ESPSW Configuration"

config ESPSW_RELAY_GPIO
    int "Relay module IN GPIO"
    range 0 23
    default 1
    help
        GPIO wired to the relay module's IN pin. Default 1 = XIAO ESP32-C6 pad D1.

config ESPSW_RELAY_ACTIVE_LOW
    bool "Relay module input is active-low (open-drain drive)"
    default y
    help
        Most 5 V optocoupler relay modules turn ON when IN is pulled to GND.
        When set, the GPIO is driven open-drain: sink = ON, Hi-Z = OFF.
        Clear this for active-high modules (H/L jumper on H): push-pull, HIGH = ON.

config ESPSW_LED_GPIO
    int "Status LED GPIO (Identify blink), -1 to disable"
    range -1 23
    default 15
    help
        XIAO ESP32-C6 onboard user LED is GPIO15, active-low.

config ESPSW_ZB_TX_POWER_DBM
    int "Zigbee transmit power (dBm)"
    range -24 20
    default 20
    help
        802.15.4 TX power. 20 dBm (the C6 maximum) draws ~300 mA bursts at 5 V during
        every transmit (link status every 15 s as a Router). Lower it to ~10 dBm if a
        weak supply shows LED dips in sync with Zigbee traffic and you cannot add bulk
        capacitance; that cuts the burst by roughly a third and is still fine indoors.

endmenu
